## (B) Third-party and upstream material — not licensed by this repository

Lumenora is built from Fedora Kinoite, an atomic KDE Plasma desktop, and from additional upstream software packages, libraries, firmware, and runtime components. Those upstream components are governed by their own licenses. This repository does not grant any license to them.

The governing license for each third-party component is the license attached to that component by its upstream author, maintainer, package metadata, or shipped license files. The controlling source for any given component is one of the following, in descending order of specificity:

* an SPDX identifier embedded in the file itself;
* the license text shipped with the component;
* the package metadata for the component;
* the upstream project’s own legal or licensing page.

Where a component is distributed in source form, binary form, or both, the obligations that apply to that component are determined by that component’s own license, not by section (A) of this notice.

### 1. Fedora base system and Fedora-derived content

The Fedora base system, Fedora package set, Fedora RPMs, Fedora documentation, and Fedora branding are separate from Lumenora’s MIT-licensed material. Each Fedora component retains its own license and trademark status.

This includes, without limitation, Fedora-provided operating-system packages, libraries, desktop components, installer content, metadata, documentation, and any other Fedora-originated material that is present in the image or build environment.

### 2. Linux kernel and kernel-derived material

The Linux kernel is licensed under GPL-2.0-only with the Linux-syscall-note exception. It is not licensed under a generic “GPL v2 or later” statement unless a particular file states otherwise.

Any kernel-derived material included in a Lumenora build, including an alternative kernel tree or a vendor fork, remains subject to the license of the upstream kernel sources and any applicable notices or exceptions that accompany those sources.

### 3. Open Gaming Collective (OGC) gaming kernel

Lumenora uses the Open Gaming Collective kernel, and that kernel remains governed by the upstream kernel license and the license terms stated by the fork’s maintainers. Lumenora does not alter those terms.

### 4. KDE Plasma, KDE Frameworks, and KDE Gear

KDE software included in a Lumenora image remains governed by the license attached to the specific KDE file, module, package, or artifact.

KDE components may include files licensed under LGPL, GPL, BSD, MIT, documentation licenses, and media or content licenses. The controlling license for each file is the license stated by that file or by the upstream KDE project.

### 5. Qt 6

Qt 6 is available under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 3 and, for some components, under the GNU General Public License version 3 or commercial terms from The Qt Company. Any Qt component included in Lumenora remains subject to the license terms that apply to that specific component.

### 6. NVIDIA drivers and NVIDIA open kernel modules

The NVIDIA proprietary driver stack, firmware, and related user-space components are distributed under NVIDIA’s own license terms and EULA. Those terms are not replaced by this repository.

The NVIDIA open GPU kernel modules, when included, remain subject to NVIDIA’s upstream terms and the license of the specific source files or binaries distributed by NVIDIA. This repository does not grant any additional rights in NVIDIA material beyond the rights NVIDIA itself grants.

### 7. Other bundled upstream software

Any other bundled software, including gamescope, MangoHud, GameMode, Steam, distrobox, fastfetch, eza, oh-my-posh, Flatpak runtimes, Flatpak applications, libraries, codecs, fonts, and firmware, remains governed by its own upstream license or license notice.

